# Line-ending policy — required for reproducible DVC hashing.
#
# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true in its system config, which checks
# text files out with CRLF. DVC hashes dependency files byte-for-byte, so a
# CRLF working tree yields different md5s than the LF content stored in git:
# every `dvc repro` on Windows then reports the stage as changed and rewrites
# dvc.lock, even when nothing was edited. Pinning LF for the file types that
# participate in DVC hashing (and in CI) keeps those hashes stable on every
# platform. These rules override core.autocrlf.

*.py      text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.toml    text eol=lf
*.dvc     text eol=lf
dvc.lock  text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.pdf     binary
